# Frosty LangGraph Backend — Comprehensive Project Report

**Project:** Frosty AI Assistant Backend  
**Company:** Frostrek LLP  
**Report Date:** 2026-03-02  
**Stack:** Python 3.14 · FastAPI · LangGraph · OpenAI GPT-4o-mini · PostgreSQL · FAISS · Google Calendar API · SMTP

---

## 1. Executive Summary

Frosty is a production-grade AI assistant backend built on **LangGraph** (stateful graph-based orchestration) with **FastAPI** as the API layer. It provides multi-modal conversational capabilities including text chat, voice input/output, email composition & sending, meeting scheduling via Google Calendar, and RAG-powered knowledge retrieval — all backed by persistent session memory in PostgreSQL.

The system is currently **functional and running locally** at `http://localhost:8000`. Recent fixes (2026-03-02) resolved a database schema issue, logging failure, and response flow reliability.

---

## 2. Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Client (Web/API)"] -->|POST /chat| B["FastAPI App (app.py)"]
    A -->|POST /api/v1/chat| B
    B --> C["chat_router (main.py)"]
    C -->|awaiting_confirmation?| D["handle_confirmation"]
    C -->|else| E["LangGraph State Machine"]
    E --> F["classify_intent_node"]
    F -->|normal_chat| G["normal_chat_node"]
    F -->|schedule_meeting| H["schedule_meeting_node"]
    F -->|send_email / send_email_only| I["email_flow_node"]
    F -->|missing_information| G
    G --> J["OpenAI GPT-4o-mini"]
    H --> K["Google Calendar API"]
    I --> L["SMTP Email"]
    F --> M["RAG Engine (FAISS)"]
    G --> M
    B --> N["chat_logger → PostgreSQL"]
    C --> O["session_store → PostgreSQL"]
```

### Request Flow

```
Client POST → FastAPI endpoint → chat_router()
  → (if awaiting_confirmation) → handle_confirmation() → return
  → (else) → LangGraph.invoke(state)
    → classify_intent_node (LLM intent + entity extraction)
    → route_by_intent
      → normal_chat_node | schedule_meeting_node | email_flow_node
  → save_session_state()
  → return api_response to client
```

